# Binaries
/bin/
/dist/
/epistemicos-api
/epistemicos-cli
# Windows: `go build ./cmd/epistemicos-cli/` emits epistemicos-cli.exe, which
# the extensionless patterns above do not cover.
/epistemicos-api.exe
/epistemicos-cli.exe

# Test artifacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.out

# Local config — NEVER commit. Contains Mathpix and database credentials.
# Glob-matched deliberately: Notepad silently saves ".env" as ".env.txt",
# which an exact-name rule would miss and `git add -A` would then stage.
.env*
!.env.example

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Local agent-tool settings (user-scoped, not project artefacts)
.claude/

# Local PDF / data volume
/data/

# Sample conversions in the working root. Anchored with a leading slash so it
# cannot reach test fixtures: internal/core/domain/segment/testdata/demo.md is
# the Step 3 reference fixture (§15) and MUST be committed. An unanchored
# `demo*.md` matched it at every depth and silently excluded it.
/demo*.md

# Python bytecode, created by running the scripts in scripts/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Working copies of reviewer replies, staged in the root on the way to `record`.
# The authoritative copy is cycle-NN/codex-output-raw.md: preserved at record
# time, hashed into target evidence, and checked by MC-2. A second copy in the
# root is checked by nothing, so an edit to it would be invisible and a later
# reader could take it for the record. Four were tracked until 17 September;
# all four were byte-identical to their cycle copies, which is luck rather than
# a property anything enforced.
/reply*.md
/codex-reply*.md
